{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976654-are-the-mundane-weapons-in-technomancers-toybox-a-bit-overkill","id":976654,"title":"Are the Mundane weapons in Technomancers toybox a bit overkill?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-26T12:17:33-07:00","id":976654,"title":"Are the Mundane weapons in Technomancers toybox a bit overkill?","content":"So, I finally got around to looking through the Hardware section of Technomancers Toybox, after remembering something Quantumboost said about rules for Talismans that don't require a dot of willpower.<br /> <br /> Wrong section of the book of course. But what the heck. These heavy weapons in the back of the book are INSANE. The 30mm Chain Guns that are mentioned all over the place in Guide to the Technocracy but have no stats? Deal 10 damage a shot and fire 42 shots a round. Or if you use the simpler rules, 15 damage a shot, and 8 shots a round. Either way is more than enough to chunk pretty much anything I have ever seen in a direct combat scenario. And considering it's relatively simple to get ahold of these heavy weapons for a Matter mage with the right skills...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T23:34:40-07:00","id":977011,"title":"","content":"Mmmh. On one hand, Technomancer's Toybox is a little old and might have some balancing issues...<br /> <br /> On the other hand, they are *<i>frickin' chainguns*</i>. Pretty much the fastest-firing objects of large-calibre delivery that humanity ever invented ( Aside of Metalstorm...and this is all still in the confines of sleeper-tech, not hypertech. ). 30mm anything are normally put on <i>heavy combat vehicles</i>. A Warthog uses it to destroy TANKS.<br /> Comparing their destructiveness to normal guns is kind of like comparing an assault rifle to a small handgun.<br /> <br /> So, their stats kind of make sense. They simply shouldn't be common, at all, and a reason why the old HIT Mark V's are so damn scary in the first place. Producing enough ammo for them to last longer than a second is another problem, as is even remotely carrying them, concealing them, or going as nuts as wielding them. No normal human can do that, and doing so is a paradox magnet galore.<br /> <br /> As for making them, unless the mage has a reeaaaally faith-driven paradigm like, heck, a Chorister, making them with matter is not easily done - It would require a Mage who's an engineer, with an intimate knowledge of military-grade weapons technology. Heck, they'd probably have to have the blueprints for one, or taken one apart before.<br /> <br /> So, no, I don't see them easy to come by at all, military and Technocrats excluded. <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Although, a little nitpick would be, I assume that 'Chaingun' here refers to a 'Gatling gun'. Chainguns usually have one barrel ( like those on an Apache helicopter) and would fire slower than the 42-shots-a-turn stats in the book.<br /> <br /> But, in the case of a gatling - those 15 and 42 shots a round in the case of a gatling gun and a 3-second combat turn would actually translate to several hundred actual bullets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-27-2016, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T04:43:33-07:00","id":977119,"title":"","content":"To add, the HIT Mark Chainguns are quite smaller than the vehicle mounted one in Technomancer's Toybox.<br /> <br /> According to M20, they're Damage 8, Rate 3, clip of 200.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T07:39:59-07:00","id":977174,"title":"","content":"I would actually suggest they are underpowered, given the probability of a human dying from one 30mm round is better than the 40% given by a base damage of 10 with one net success. I think that base damage should be around 15, meaning that a normal human would have around a 60% of dying if hit by one round with one net success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T11:54:26-07:00","id":977278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976654-are-the-mundane-weapons-in-technomancers-toybox-a-bit-overkill?p=977174#post977174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would actually suggest they are underpowered, given the probability of a human dying from one 30mm round is better than the 40% given by a base damage of 10 with one net success. I think that base damage should be around 15, meaning that a normal human would have around a 60% of dying if hit by one round with one net success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that taking aiming difficulty due to recoil into account?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T12:49:07-07:00","id":977314,"title":"","content":"We are assuming one net success for the purpose of calculating damage for a single shot only. Recoil is generally only a factor when you have multiple shots within a given time period (cWoD never had particularly good recoil rules because they rewarded auto fire with greater accuracy, which is just absurd given that nature of firearms). A 30mm round is a massive round, over twice as large and ten times as masdive as a .50 caliber round, which would mean that it should make normal humans very, very dead unless it blew off a limb (a normal human could potentially survive losing a limb to a 30mm round if they received medical attention before they bled to death). Auto fire of such a weapon is a waste against anything smaller than a fighter jet or a tank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T16:07:26-07:00","id":977450,"title":"","content":"And it seems like some *sleeper* company is working on a prototype of a HIT Mark Microgun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vj0lxQyL7ZQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vj0lxQyL7ZQ\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vj0lxQyL7ZQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vj0lxQyL7ZQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> NATO 5.56 calibre. Also, a first glance might mislead..but if you count, that's about 75 casings on the table afterwards.<br /> <br /> The timetable is advancing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T16:11:13-07:00","id":977456,"title":"","content":"They have been playing with that type of stuff for over twenty years. The main problem is waste heat, the heat from firing can start cooking off the remaining rounds, which is a bad thing. However, material technology continues to improve, so old designs start becoming feasible with new materials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T16:42:22-07:00","id":977468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/976654-are-the-mundane-weapons-in-technomancers-toybox-a-bit-overkill?p=977456#post977456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have been playing with that type of stuff for over twenty years. The main problem is waste heat, the heat from firing can start cooking off the remaining rounds, which is a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Statistical Inevitability sure is a pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}